<protocol name="image_studio" type="tool_mastery" domain="shared">

## PURPOSE

Professional image processing with Gemini 3 Pro Image.
Transform uploads into catalog-ready assets.

---

## LABELED IMAGES

Each image has a label you reference in specs:

```json
{"images": [
  {"path": "[source_path]", "label": "source"},
  {"path": "[reference_path]", "label": "style_ref"}
]}
```

Reference in specs: `"extract [source]"`, `"match [style_ref] lighting"`

| Label | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| source / product | Main item to process |
| style_ref | Lighting/mood reference |
| background | Scene reference |
| variant | Additional product for family shots |

**Max 15 images per call.**

---

## SPECS QUICK REFERENCE

Use what applies. All optional. All accept free-form strings.

| Spec | Key Fields | When |
|------|------------|------|
| **fidelity** | preserve_colors, preserve_artwork, hero_features | ALWAYS for source products |
| **extraction** | target_description, isolation, edge_treatment | Isolating from background |
| **background** | treatment (transparent/solid/scene), color | Setting background |
| **lighting** | type, direction, special_requirements | Controlling light |
| **material_treatment** | primary_material, rendering_notes | Glass/metal/specialty |
| **composition** | product_coverage, position, camera_angle | Framing |
| **scene** | environment, style, mood | Lifestyle generation |
| **placement** | position, scale, surface | Product in scene |
| **output** | format, size, aspect_ratio, filename | Output specs |

**Fidelity is MANDATORY when processing source products.**

---

## PATTERNS

Adapt these to your context. Never copy specific values.

### Catalog Hero

```
images: [source]
specs: extraction + background (white) + fidelity + material_treatment
result: Clean product on white, identity preserved
```

### Lifestyle Scene

```
images: [product] + optional [style_ref]
specs: scene + placement + lighting + fidelity
result: Product in environment, photorealistic
```

### Multi-Item Individual

```
images: [source with N items]
loop: For each item, extraction targeting "[description] at [position]"
result: N separate outputs
```

### Family Composition

```
images: [main] + [variant1] + [variant2]
specs: composition ("[main] center, [variants] supporting") + background
result: Family shot
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Don't | Why | Instead |
|-------|-----|---------|
| Skip view_image before | Process blind | Always see source first |
| Skip fidelity spec | Identity loss | Always include for products |
| Skip material_treatment for glass/metal | Flat rendering | Specify material |
| Copy example values | Wrong for your context | Adapt to what you SEE |
| Single extraction for multi-item | 1 asset instead of N | Extract each separately |
| Ignore storage_path output | Can't create asset record | Capture for write_data |

---

## OUTPUT

### Success
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "storage_path": "pending/[filename].png",
  "metadata": {"width": N, "height": N, "format": "..."}
}
```

Use `storage_path` for write_data asset records.

### Error
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "...",
  "error_code": "FILE_NOT_FOUND | API_ERROR | ...",
  "next_steps": ["..."]
}
```

---

## WORKFLOW

```
view_image (see source) -> image_studio (process) -> view_image (verify) -> write_data (catalog)
```

</protocol>
